Upstream silnrsi/grcompiler commits 21532df935 and 1bb05131be (Tim Eves,
2024-03-13, "Fix FTBFS for GrcRgressionTest in gcc on Ubuntu Noble"),
unchanged and applied in order. Not in any release: v5.2.1 (2021) is the
latest tag.

GrcRegressionTest's main.h uses uint32_t without including <cstdint>; GCC
13 and later no longer pull it in transitively:

  CompareFontTables.cpp:448:9: error: 'uint32_t' was not declared in this scope

The test binary is built by the default target (test/ is an unconditional
add_subdirectory), so this breaks the whole build.

diff --git a/test/GrcRegressionTest/main.h b/test/GrcRegressionTest/main.h
index 334aa0d..4892780 100644
--- a/test/GrcRegressionTest/main.h
+++ b/test/GrcRegressionTest/main.h
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ Responsibility: Sharon Correll
 //:>********************************************************************************************
 //:>	Include files
 //:>********************************************************************************************
+#include <cstddef>
 #ifdef _WIN32
 #include <windows.h>
 #endif // _WIN32
diff --git a/test/GrcRegressionTest/main.h b/test/GrcRegressionTest/main.h
index 4892780..24149f3 100644
--- a/test/GrcRegressionTest/main.h
+++ b/test/GrcRegressionTest/main.h
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ Responsibility: Sharon Correll
 //:>********************************************************************************************
 //:>	Include files
 //:>********************************************************************************************
-#include <cstddef>
+#include <cstdint>
 #ifdef _WIN32
 #include <windows.h>
 #endif // _WIN32
